.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt KAI 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kai
.Nd a dock for Hyprland
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op command
.Op Fl Fl replace
.Op Fl Fl software | Fl Fl opengl
.Nm
.Cm settings
.Nm
.Cm apps
.Nm
.Cm quit
.Nm
.Cm theme
.Cm list | install Ar FILE | apply Ar ID
.Op Fl Fl json
.Nm
.Fl Fl version | Fl Fl help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a classic, full-featured dock for the
.Xr hyprland 1
compositor, in the spirit of Cairo-Dock: a floating shelf along one screen
edge with parabolic zoom, reflections and icon animations, pinned launchers
and running apps, live applets that can also float on the desktop as
desklets, and one-click themes with fine-tuning.
.Pp
It speaks the layer-shell protocol, follows the Omarchy accent and
Hyprland's rounding unless a theme overrides them, and talks to Hyprland
over its IPC sockets for the window list and for focus, minimize, close
and launch dispatching.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It (no command)
Start the dock. If a dock is already running, Settings open in the running
instance instead.
.It Cm settings
Open Settings in the running dock.
.It Cm apps
Open the app launcher, a searchable grid of every installed app, or close
it if it is open. Type to filter, move with the arrow keys, launch with
Enter, close with Esc.
.It Cm quit
Quit the running dock.
.It Cm theme Cm list Op Fl Fl json
List installed themes; the applied one is marked.
.It Cm theme Cm install Ar FILE Op Fl Fl json
Install a theme from a JSON file (an https address or a path also works
from Settings).
.It Cm theme Cm apply Ar ID Op Fl Fl json
Apply an installed theme.
.It Fl Fl replace
Start a new dock instead of talking to the running one.
.It Fl Fl software
Start with the software (CPU) renderer this run; useful when the GPU
driver crashes or flickers. Persisted in the config until the other flag
is used.
.It Fl Fl opengl
Start with the OpenGL (hardware) renderer this run.
.It Fl Fl version , Fl Fl help
Print the version or the usage text.
.El
.Pp
The
.Cm theme
commands run without a display, so scripts and agents can use them.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Settings live in
.Pa ~/.config/kai/config.json
and are edited through the Settings window, which opens with
.Nm settings
or by running
.Nm
again while the dock runs. Themes live in
.Pa ~/.local/share/kai/themes/
and the current one is stored as
.Dq theme
with per-setting
.Dq themeOverrides
on top. The interface language follows
.Pa ~/.config/omarchy/language .
.Pp
Key settings:
.Bl -tag -width "currentWorkspaceOnly"
.It Cm edge , Cm screen
Which screen edge the dock sits on and which monitor.
.It Cm view
"floating" shelf, full-width "panel", or icons standing on a 3D "plane";
empty lets the theme decide.
.It Cm iconSize , Cm zoom , Cm zoomRange , Cm spacing , Cm margin
Icon size in pixels, magnification and its reach, icon spacing and the
gap from the screen edge.
.It Cm layer , Cm autohide , Cm autohideDelay , Cm reserveSpace
Layer-shell layer, whether the dock slides away when the pointer leaves
and after how long, and whether maximized windows keep clear of it.
.It Cm clickAnimation , Cm hoverAnimation , Cm launchAnimation , Cm attentionAnimation , Cm animationSpeed
Which animation plays when an icon is clicked, when the pointer enters
it, while an app starts, when a window wants attention, and how fast
they run. One of bounce, pulse, flip, wobble, blink or none.
.It Cm separators
List of dock elements after which a separator line is drawn: the string
.Ql launcher
for the apps launcher or a pinned app id such as
.Ql firefox .
Empty keeps the default lines.
.It Cm showRunning , Cm currentWorkspaceOnly , Cm clickActiveMinimizes
Whether unpinned running apps appear, only from the current workspace,
and whether clicking the focused app minimizes it.
.It Cm clockAnalog , Cm clock24h , Cm clockSeconds , Cm clockFont , Cm clockFontScale
Clock face: analog or digital, 12 or 24 hours, seconds, and the digital
face's font family and size multiplier.
.It Cm weatherCity , Cm weatherUnits
The Open-Meteo city and metric or imperial units.
.El
.Sh APPLETS
Six applets can live in the dock or on the desktop as desklets: the
.Ql apps
launcher, a
.Ql clock
that opens a month calendar when clicked,
.Ql weather
with a three-day forecast,
.Ql sysmon
with CPU and memory graphs,
.Ql battery ,
and the
.Ql trash .
Detach an applet from its right-click menu to drop it on the desktop;
hover a desklet to put it back. Dragging an applet reorders the dock.
The apps launcher opens the Omarchy menu, with wofi, fuzzel and walker
as fallbacks.
.Sh AUTOSTART
Add to
.Pa ~/.config/hypr/autostart.lua :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
o.launch_on_start("/home/user/Work/kai/build/kai")
.Ed
.Pp
(adjust the path to where kai is installed) and the dock starts with the
compositor.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.local/share/kai/themes/" -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/kai/config.json
Settings.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/kai/themes/
Installed themes.
.It Pa ~/.config/omarchy/language
Interface language.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on success, 1 on a failed command such as an unknown theme.
